  {
    "name": "N4 ONME2 only needs the executable root to be historical",
    "file": "compiler/src/onme.cpp",
    "old": "&&authorRoot==rootOf(p,IdentityProjection::Onme2Compatibility);",
    "new": ";",
    "tests": [
      "tests/cp15_projection.py",
      "HistoricalIdentityTests"
    ],
    "equivalent": "The second conjunct of the ONME2 decision compares the HISTORICAL root of the authoring program with its current root. The executable is validate(parseWave(wave(p))) and the system node of a program carries wave(p): when the Wave of a program is a fixed point of its own reading, p and the executable have the same projection in every identity mode, so authorRoot==legacyAuthor holds exactly when execRoot==legacyExec holds and the conjunct adds nothing. That fixed point is what tests/cp15_scale.py (reads_back_everywhere, 17 programs) and tools/survey_roundtrip.py (86 repository programs, 0 mismatches) assert; the authoring and the executable root are equal in all 86 valid programs of the repository. A program for which they differ would be a defect of the Wave round trip, not of this decision."
  },
